From e6f2528b07299bbc66a00d1d3b1f32ff3a4398e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:48:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] freedreno: round up the NV12 chroma plane size

For odd widths or heights the UV plane of a single-BO NV12 resource is
sized from width0 / 2 and height0 / 2, one chroma sample short of what
4:2:0 needs. With UBWC this also gives a different layout than the one
the display controller and the video codecs use, which round up: at
some sizes the UV metadata is a page smaller, so the scanout fetches
the chroma from the wrong offset, and at widths of 128n + 1 the UV
pitch is 128 bytes narrower than the Y pitch.

Round the chroma plane up, as DRM and V4L2 do for subsampled planes.

Fixes: 266f1d948a4a ("freedreno: allocate NV12 Y and UV planes into a single GEM BO")
Cc: mesa-stable
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
index 29134ba1337..2b498f6baf1 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
@@ -1517,8 +1517,8 @@ fd_resource_create_with_modifiers(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
         tmpl->format == PIPE_FORMAT_Y8_U8V8_420_UNORM)) {
       struct pipe_resource uv_tmpl = *tmpl;
       uv_tmpl.format = PIPE_FORMAT_R8G8_UNORM;
-      uv_tmpl.width0 = tmpl->width0 / 2;
-      uv_tmpl.height0 = tmpl->height0 / 2;
+      uv_tmpl.width0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(tmpl->width0, 2);
+      uv_tmpl.height0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(tmpl->height0, 2);
 
       uint32_t uv_size = 0;
       uv_prsc = fd_resource_allocate_and_resolve(pscreen, &uv_tmpl, modifiers, count, &uv_size);

From b39942def326447fb4b780ad167d2f34d1e5fe8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:10:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dri: round up the subsampled plane size on dma-buf import

When a planar YUV dma-buf with an odd width or height is imported, the
subsampled planes are created with the size shifted down, one chroma
sample short of what the producer allocated. This results in the
information loss. This contradics with the other code handling
dimensions. FOr example, util_format_get_plane_width/height() rounds up.
In the kernel, drm_format_info_plane_width/height() also rounds
dimensions up.

Round the plane size up, as util_format_get_plane_width() and DRM do.

Fixes: ecd6fce2611e ("mesa/st: support lowering multi-planar YUV")
Cc: mesa-stable
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
index 4846d9c1c7e..b8b732c2bd8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
@@ -750,8 +750,8 @@ dri_create_image_from_winsys(struct dri_screen *screen,
       struct pipe_resource *tex;
 
       templ.next = img->texture;
-      templ.width0 = width >> map->planes[i].width_shift;
-      templ.height0 = height >> map->planes[i].height_shift;
+      templ.width0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(width, 1 << map->planes[i].width_shift);
+      templ.height0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(height, 1 << map->planes[i].height_shift);
       if (use_lowered)
          templ.format = map->planes[i].dri_format;
       else
